# D&D Campaign Management - Cursor Rules

## CRITICAL SAFETY RULES

### NO-LOOKUP PLAY RULES
- When running D&D sessions, NEVER use web search or external lookups during active play
- All game mechanics, rules, and content must come from local files only
- Do NOT interrupt gameplay with external API calls or searches
- Maintain immersion by using only pre-loaded campaign data

### STRICT OUTPUT BLOCKS
- All code blocks MUST use proper citation format for existing code
- Use `startLine:endLine:filepath` format for code references
- Use standard markdown code blocks for new/proposed code
- NEVER mix formats or include line numbers in code content
- NEVER indent triple backticks

### CAMPAIGN DATA PROTECTION
- Campaign data in `C:\DnD\Campaigns\Phandelver` is NEVER to be Git-tracked
- NEVER run destructive Git commands that could affect campaign data
- Campaign data MUST remain outside any Git repository, worktree, or OneDrive
- Always verify file paths before any Git operations

### SECRETS PROTECTION
- NEVER commit secrets: OpenAI_Key.txt, google_credentials.json, .env, *.key, *.pem, *.pfx
- Always check .gitignore before committing
- If ambiguous, choose the safest option (don't commit secrets)

### PARALLEL AGENT PROTECTION
- Ignore all parallel agent temp outputs: .coord-*/, .cursor-worktrees/, .agent-id, .session-id
- These are automatically ignored via .gitignore

### WORKTREE PROTECTION
- NEVER create worktrees that include campaign data
- Campaign data MUST remain in `C:\DnD\Campaigns\Phandelver` (outside all repos)
- If creating worktrees, ensure they only contain code, not campaign data

### FILE OPERATIONS
- Before deleting files, verify they are not campaign data
- Before moving files, verify destination is safe
- When in doubt, ask or choose the safest option

### CHARACTER DATA VERIFICATION
- When loading character abilities for combat, always read through character sheet files
- Verify exact abilities, spells, and features from actual character data
- Do not assume abilities based on class alone - check the actual character data
- Reference the dungeon master text document, monster manual, and players manual before making decisions

### OUTPUT FORMATTING
- Use proper code citation format: ```startLine:endLine:filepath
- Include at least 1 line of actual code in any reference block
- Never include line numbers in code content
- Triple backticks must start at column 0 (never indented)

### GENERAL SAFETY
- If anything is ambiguous, choose the safest option
- Don't touch campaign data unless explicitly requested
- Don't run destructive git commands without explicit confirmation
- Always verify paths and operations before execution

